      "id": "aot-fib-recursive",
      "tier": "aot",
      "profile": "aot_wasi",
      "input": "tests/conformance/benchmarks/fib_recursive.pns",
      "expected": {
        "status": "success",
        "exit_code": 0,
        "stdout": "832040\n",
        "result": "832040",
        "deviation": {
          "id": "DEV-004",
          "rationale": "This tier exercises the SEPARATE MIR->WASM AOT pipeline (panos build --target=wasm, T043/T048), not the bytecode VM the `runtime` tier above uses — same source, same result, but a genuinely different execution path (no Odin equivalent exists to compare against: Odin never built a MIR-based AOT backend for this migration, see docs/src/architecture/toolchain-and-testing.md's MIR/WASM section). `stdout` here is the raw `wasmtime run --invoke старт` process output (includes wasmtime's own trailing newline), not the bytecode VM CLI's rendered value — the two tiers are not byte-for-byte comparable outcomes, only value-equal."
        }
      }
    },
